From 07a691ab939d1e4d76000b020cf776332e2fe150 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:04:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/33] generate: STRATA_CKPT_POOL=1 saves checkpoints into
 dropped ones' vectors, STRATA_CKPT_THREADS=1 saves a split's parts at once

STRATA_CKPT_POOL=1 (off by default): the serve loop keeps the running-state
vectors of the checkpoints it drops (LRU eviction, the tail one, the prune at
a new request, a batch slot's old one), at most two, and the next checkpoint
or slot copy goes into them.  A save then resizes nothing: no zero-fill of
~118 MB of fresh vectors.  Every byte is overwritten by the copy.

STRATA_CKPT_THREADS=1 (off by default): a layer split's checkpoint saves the
first stage's part on the calling thread and every later stage's on a
persistent thread of its own (the copies' private streams are per thread, so
short-lived threads would leak them).  The threads leave the host thread's one
CPU first (to the aux CPUs with --aux-cpus, else to every CPU the process may
use): on it the copies only took turns.

Measured on a 4-stage split (T16, 24 batch admissions per arm): a turn
checkpoint takes 17.2 ms today, 10.4 ms with the pool and 5.6 ms with both;
the batch tests, the overlap and interleave tests and a driver run give the
same tokens with the switches on as off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
